WEBVTT

00:06.673 --> 00:09.300
[sweet airy music]

00:50.341 --> 00:52.260
[Ung] You see, the thing about dating

00:52.927 --> 00:55.096
is that it's like living
in a different world.

00:56.639 --> 00:58.141
Most especially

00:58.933 --> 01:00.477
dating Yeon-su

01:00.977 --> 01:03.813
is a completely different world.

01:06.024 --> 01:08.026
[Yeon-su] Ung!

01:08.109 --> 01:08.943
[Ung] Yeah?

01:09.736 --> 01:10.695
What?

01:12.280 --> 01:13.239
What is it?

01:17.494 --> 01:19.245
- Why'd you call me?
- It's your bedtime.

01:19.329 --> 01:20.413
Hmm?

01:21.331 --> 01:23.541
I can't sleep now. It's only 10 p.m.

01:26.961 --> 01:29.964
I drank all the jujube tea.
Where did you get this from?

01:30.632 --> 01:33.468
- Does this house have a well?
- Drink it and go to bed.

01:34.093 --> 01:37.680
Uh, I don't sleep at this hour.
Even kids don't sleep this early.

01:37.764 --> 01:39.766
So should I sleep here then?

01:40.391 --> 01:42.310
[cheery music]

01:42.393 --> 01:45.480
- [gulping]
- [chuckles]

01:46.189 --> 01:47.148
[sighs]

01:47.899 --> 01:49.567
We should sleep when it's dark.

01:49.651 --> 01:52.278
It's dangerous for you
to walk around at this late hour.

01:52.362 --> 01:53.822
[chuckles]

01:55.281 --> 01:56.449
- Let's go to bed.
- [chuckles]

01:56.533 --> 01:59.119
[panting]

01:59.702 --> 02:00.578
Come on!

02:00.662 --> 02:02.163
- Wake up!
- [groans]

02:02.247 --> 02:04.958
Make up your mind.
Do you want me to sleep or not?

02:05.041 --> 02:07.460
You can't sleep at night
because you sleep in the morning.

02:07.544 --> 02:10.338
You have to endure this
to get a normal sleep cycle.

02:10.421 --> 02:11.339
Okay?

02:11.422 --> 02:13.383
- [Ung groaning]
- [panting]

02:13.466 --> 02:15.218
[Ung] But as you're all aware,

02:15.301 --> 02:17.637
that world isn't really a good fit for me.

02:19.347 --> 02:21.141
But hey, what can I do?

02:21.224 --> 02:23.268
Oh, the bus is here. See you around.

02:23.351 --> 02:24.727
Oh, wait, Yeon-su!

02:28.606 --> 02:29.691
See you.

02:29.774 --> 02:31.234
- Yeon-su.
- Yeah?

02:32.694 --> 02:34.154
- [both chuckling]
- Bye.

02:36.239 --> 02:38.324
[cheerful music]

02:47.667 --> 02:48.543
What's up?

02:49.252 --> 02:51.379
I just got back home after work.

02:51.462 --> 02:53.673
You got off work late.
Did you have dinner already?

02:53.756 --> 02:56.050
Mm-hmm, I ate at the place
you recommended to me,

02:56.134 --> 02:57.051
and it was pretty good.

02:57.135 --> 02:59.637
- Let's go there next time.
- Okay, let's do that.

02:59.721 --> 03:02.348
- [Ung] Back then and even now…
- [chuckles]

03:03.516 --> 03:05.685
[gentle sweet music]

03:09.981 --> 03:12.025
…I want to keep living in this world.

03:14.277 --> 03:15.612
A world without an end,

03:16.613 --> 03:17.572
forever.

03:19.073 --> 03:19.991
[Yeon-su] No.

03:20.074 --> 03:21.743
But you're the only one

03:22.577 --> 03:23.953
that I can get rid of.

03:24.037 --> 03:25.455
[Ung] Give me a reason.

03:26.164 --> 03:28.541
[shouting] Give me just one reason
why we can't be together!

03:32.462 --> 03:34.839
- [sighs]
- [pensive music]

03:36.591 --> 03:38.051
Those are useless thoughts.

03:40.929 --> 03:43.014
LIKE WATER FOR CHOCOLATE

03:45.391 --> 03:47.435
[Yeon-su] In times like these,
I have to be more cautious.

03:47.518 --> 03:48.603
THE LIKELIHOOD OF STAYING IN
A RELATIONSHIP WITH YOUR EX

03:48.686 --> 03:51.814
Because misfortune always comes
disguised as happiness.

03:54.275 --> 03:59.239
"Couples who fight often have
a higher chance of dating again."

04:01.241 --> 04:06.120
"However, they think that they will still
be the same after they get back together

04:06.788 --> 04:09.123
and have lower expectations
of each other."

04:10.041 --> 04:12.043
"In order to maintain your relationship,

04:12.627 --> 04:16.130
you must show your partner
new sides of yourself

04:16.214 --> 04:20.551
to break such expectations.
This is necessary."

04:23.346 --> 04:26.516
I shouldn't lower my ground
just because everything is okay.

04:27.809 --> 04:32.230
So I believe that I have to prepare myself
for any possible risks that might happen.

04:32.897 --> 04:35.149
"New sides of myself…"

04:35.233 --> 04:36.484
I went through so much to get here.

04:38.945 --> 04:41.114
I can't repeat the same mistakes again.

04:41.197 --> 04:43.116
[both chuckling]

04:45.576 --> 04:47.578
[bright cheerful music]

04:47.662 --> 04:49.872
[broom rasping]

04:55.795 --> 05:00.967
EPISODE 13

05:04.429 --> 05:06.472
[suspenseful music]

05:07.265 --> 05:09.309
[sighs]
I wanna stay with you forever.

05:10.059 --> 05:11.686
[chuckles]
Come here.

05:12.603 --> 05:14.897
[suspenseful music continues]

05:23.364 --> 05:24.449
What do we do?

05:25.742 --> 05:27.744
I'll deal with him. You go to work.

05:27.827 --> 05:28.703
What will you do?

05:29.329 --> 05:31.039
Is there a brick here somewhere?

05:31.748 --> 05:34.042
Take care of this quietly
so there's no fuss.

05:34.125 --> 05:36.252
- Mm. Hmm.
- Bye.

05:37.003 --> 05:39.047
[cheeky suspenseful music]

05:42.258 --> 05:43.634
[deep sigh]

05:44.844 --> 05:46.721
Ung… Ung…

05:49.015 --> 05:52.435
Hey, inhale with your nose,
exhale through your mouth.

05:53.144 --> 05:56.564
[deep breaths]

05:56.647 --> 05:58.191
[both breathe heavily]

05:59.734 --> 06:01.486
What… what was that about?

06:02.361 --> 06:03.196
It just happened.

06:03.863 --> 06:05.031
"It just happened"?

06:05.114 --> 06:06.532
Hey, don't overreact.

06:07.617 --> 06:10.745
Wait, since when?
Since when have you been doing this?

06:11.829 --> 06:13.873
So you didn't let me come
to your house because…

06:14.791 --> 06:17.043
No, forget all that.

06:17.126 --> 06:19.420
Who else knows about this?
Does Ji-ung know?

06:21.672 --> 06:23.007
And what about Sol-i?

06:24.258 --> 06:25.134
Probably.

06:26.719 --> 06:30.056
- And what about your parents?
- Yeah, they know.

06:30.890 --> 06:34.227
- Wait, is that even important?
- I'm ashamed, you know.

06:34.310 --> 06:37.688
Ashamed. How could you
not tell me about any of this?

06:38.189 --> 06:39.023
How could you?

06:39.607 --> 06:41.776
- [Ung] Are you crying?
- How could you do this?

06:42.401 --> 06:45.238
- [Eun-ho] I can't believe this!
- Have you lost it? Eun-ho!

06:47.031 --> 06:48.366
Good morning, everyone.

06:48.449 --> 06:49.992
- Good morning, Ms. Kook.
- Good morning.

06:52.203 --> 06:54.664
Hey, you think
she's going to text him again?

06:54.747 --> 06:56.624
- [Ye-in] Keep it down.
- [Ji-un] I think she will.

06:57.333 --> 07:00.711
[Ung] I couldn't take care of Eun-ho.
I'll wait for my next chance.

07:07.176 --> 07:08.594
- [Yi-hoon] Ms. Kook.
- [gasps]

07:09.345 --> 07:10.513
[Yeon-su] Oh, Mr. Bang.

07:11.180 --> 07:13.099
So tell me, do you have good news?

07:13.599 --> 07:15.393
Oh, no, there's nothing.

07:15.476 --> 07:17.728
But a double negative makes a positive.

07:18.729 --> 07:20.690
Hold on. Why are you whispering?

07:22.358 --> 07:24.902
There have been rumors going around.

07:25.736 --> 07:26.821
[gulps, inhales]

07:26.904 --> 07:28.156
What kind of rumors?

07:28.656 --> 07:31.534
Rumors of you dating someone.

07:31.617 --> 07:33.202
[chokes and coughs]

07:33.286 --> 07:34.787
[cheeky music]

07:35.621 --> 07:36.998
[clears throat]

07:38.416 --> 07:39.792
Who would say that?

07:42.044 --> 07:45.047
No, it's all right.
Don't get worked up over it. Okay?

07:45.131 --> 07:48.426
The rumors were so terrible sounding
that I told everyone it wasn't true.

07:49.010 --> 07:50.136
"Ms. Kook isn't someone like that."

07:50.219 --> 07:52.930
"She's not someone
who has any love for humanity."

07:53.014 --> 07:54.974
"Therefore, she's not human."

07:55.558 --> 07:57.185
[goofy chuckle]

07:57.268 --> 07:58.811
That's not why I'm here, though.

07:59.479 --> 08:02.732
I received a call from Soen, they asked
if they could check the footage.

08:02.815 --> 08:06.068
To be exact, the one of the project
they filmed for the documentary.

08:06.152 --> 08:08.029
Yes, and I'm quite curious too.

08:08.112 --> 08:10.490
They must have filmed our company as well.

08:10.573 --> 08:11.991
Yes, I'll ask them about it.

08:12.074 --> 08:14.744
When does it premier again?
I assume it's going to be soon?

08:15.786 --> 08:19.123
Oh, by the way,
I did an interview with them.

08:19.207 --> 08:21.334
Tell them to please let it air

08:21.417 --> 08:23.920
without editing it out, okay?

08:24.754 --> 08:25.880
[goofy chuckle]

08:25.963 --> 08:26.797
Very good.

08:32.094 --> 08:34.013
- [door opens]
- [bag thuds]

08:35.014 --> 08:35.890
[door closes]

08:39.769 --> 08:41.020
KIM JI-UNG

08:41.604 --> 08:43.397
[dial tone]

08:44.941 --> 08:47.568
[system] The person you're calling
is unavailable…

08:50.112 --> 08:54.075
HOW IS EDITING GOING?

08:57.078 --> 08:58.788
- I guess he's busy.
- [phone thuds]

09:01.290 --> 09:02.250
[sighs]

09:02.333 --> 09:05.169
[Yeon-su] Well, we could agree
on a schedule for that.

09:06.504 --> 09:07.630
The question though, is…

09:07.713 --> 09:09.465
will he be able to do it?

09:10.633 --> 09:12.426
END OF FIRST DRAFT
PREVIEW TO BE ADDED

09:14.011 --> 09:14.929
[inhales]

09:17.848 --> 09:18.724
PD. Kim.

09:20.893 --> 09:22.645
I see you've found your direction.

09:24.939 --> 09:26.983
If this is the first draft,
it'll be great.

09:28.067 --> 09:31.404
Good job. I always knew
that you could do it.

09:31.487 --> 09:33.864
I'm going to fix the last narration part.
I don't like it.

09:33.948 --> 09:35.032
Sure, go ahead.

09:35.116 --> 09:37.702
Hey, how come they look like
they haven't changed a single bit, huh?

09:37.785 --> 09:39.203
They both seem so young and lively.

09:39.287 --> 09:42.999
And there's some tension between them too.
I'm curious about the next episode.

09:43.082 --> 09:44.792
All right. I'm satisfied.

09:45.418 --> 09:46.252
That's a relief.

09:47.336 --> 09:48.963
Now stop chasing me around for it.

09:49.046 --> 09:50.172
[Dong-il] All right.

09:50.256 --> 09:53.634
It's not normal for the leader
to beg his team to see their work.

09:53.718 --> 09:55.219
Do you think so? How about you?

09:56.220 --> 09:58.014
- [phone buzzing]
- [Dong-il] It's ridiculous.

09:58.097 --> 10:00.141
Now then, what are you doing after work?

10:00.224 --> 10:03.185
We should celebrate.
After all, the first draft is finished.

10:03.269 --> 10:04.520
I still have work to do.

10:05.104 --> 10:07.773
Hey, what could be so urgent?
Let's have fun!

10:07.857 --> 10:10.901
The leader shouldn't be saying that.
I'm going to the editing room.

10:14.113 --> 10:15.448
[door opens]

10:16.240 --> 10:17.199
[door closes]

10:19.410 --> 10:20.244
Is he okay?

10:21.078 --> 10:22.413
[Chae-ran] Huh?

10:23.122 --> 10:24.290
Did you see his eyes?

10:25.333 --> 10:26.959
He seems to have lost his mind.

10:29.253 --> 10:31.714
Make sure he eats his meal on time.

10:31.797 --> 10:34.800
You should be eating well
when you're hurting inside.

10:34.884 --> 10:37.386
Got it. I'll make sure he eats well.

10:37.970 --> 10:42.016
Hey, you, you should be taking care of me.
I've been feeling so lonely lately.

10:42.099 --> 10:43.976
I'm always wandering around by myself.

10:44.060 --> 10:46.646
And what's wrong with Ji-ung?
He's just busy.

10:46.729 --> 10:50.149
He thinks he's the only one
with a lot of work? We all do!

10:50.232 --> 10:51.192
EDITING ROOM

10:51.817 --> 10:54.070
[gentle music]

10:57.490 --> 10:58.407
[door clicks]

11:10.169 --> 11:12.254
[gentle music continues]

11:18.928 --> 11:22.181
Can you tell us
what the new special documentary is about?

11:22.264 --> 11:24.642
Next year is my tenth debut anniversary.

11:24.725 --> 11:28.646
To commemorate the occasion, I'm preparing
a special video to show all of my fans.

11:28.729 --> 11:30.815
So it has been ten years already.

11:30.898 --> 11:34.151
[interviewer] Oh, you must be feeling
so many emotions right now.

11:35.111 --> 11:36.862
Yes, I do.

11:37.822 --> 11:39.698
I have quite a lot on my mind.

11:39.782 --> 11:45.037
Now, lastly, I do believe that a lot
of people are quite curious about this--

11:45.121 --> 11:46.080
The scandal?

11:46.163 --> 11:47.331
[chuckles]

11:47.415 --> 11:50.501
I hope you don't mind.
I know this may be a sensitive topic,

11:50.584 --> 11:53.379
but could you reveal anything about that
to the viewers of Litte

11:53.462 --> 11:55.548
who are watching this show live right now?

11:55.631 --> 11:57.508
Sure. I don't see any harm in it.

11:57.591 --> 11:58.634
[chuckles]

11:58.717 --> 12:02.346
Is there any truth to the rumors
that your two are dating right now?

12:02.430 --> 12:04.849
No, we aren't dating.

12:06.434 --> 12:07.435
But I do like him.

12:09.061 --> 12:11.897
- What?
- As a fan, of course.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.315
Oh.

12:13.399 --> 12:16.444
At first, he said
that he was a big fan of mine.

12:16.527 --> 12:18.737
But it turns out, I'm the bigger fan.

12:18.821 --> 12:20.489
So I wanted to become his friend,

12:21.323 --> 12:24.535
but I feel we became awkward
after the article came out.

12:26.495 --> 12:30.291
So to everyone watching,
don't make accusations about us.

12:30.374 --> 12:31.667
That's all I ask of you.

12:33.085 --> 12:35.212
So NJ was a victim of all this.

12:35.796 --> 12:37.256
And all because of that traitor.

12:37.339 --> 12:38.966
Hey, stay on one stance.

12:39.049 --> 12:42.136
If you're going to be angry,
do it at home. Why are you even here?

12:42.761 --> 12:46.265
Well, I'm here to do my job,
so I have to breathe the same air as you.

12:46.932 --> 12:49.810
By the way, how are the preparations
for your exhibition coming along?

12:50.394 --> 12:53.105
I got a lot done.
Am I ever behind schedule?

12:55.274 --> 12:57.860
Okay, what is it?
What are you even looking at?

12:59.153 --> 13:00.821
- Well, who knows?
- What?

13:00.905 --> 13:03.782
You could neglect your drawings,
after all, you're dating.

13:04.450 --> 13:07.036
- Stop that.
- Can you even focus on your work?

13:07.119 --> 13:09.872
I know that you're the kind
to neglect everything when you're dating.

13:09.955 --> 13:11.540
- Eun-ho, stop it--
- I don't get it.

13:11.624 --> 13:14.460
I just don't get
why you're seeing Yeon-su again.

13:14.543 --> 13:15.377
What?

13:15.461 --> 13:18.130
You were in so much pain.
Do you wanna repeat it?

13:18.214 --> 13:21.008
[Eun-ho] Did you forget how many times
you went through this?

13:21.091 --> 13:23.886
Do I have to remind you
how bad things got each time?

13:24.470 --> 13:27.097
I don't want to go through that again.

13:29.892 --> 13:32.186
[awkward music]

13:36.607 --> 13:37.441
What?

13:38.526 --> 13:39.527
Hey.

13:42.196 --> 13:44.281
[awkward music continues]

13:46.992 --> 13:50.788
Come on, don't say it like that.
It's fine. I'll take care of myself.

13:51.747 --> 13:54.542
How should I believe you?
You weren't going to tell me anyway.

13:54.625 --> 13:56.710
I'm really sorry about that.

13:56.794 --> 13:58.379
But I… I…

13:59.171 --> 14:00.089
[sighs]

14:01.090 --> 14:03.175
It's just, I was such
in a good mood lately.

14:04.552 --> 14:06.679
I'm so happy right now. What can I do?

14:11.100 --> 14:12.977
Oh, gross.

14:13.060 --> 14:14.228
[gags]

14:14.728 --> 14:16.897
Well, things will be different this time.

14:16.981 --> 14:18.607
I won't mess this up, okay?

14:24.154 --> 14:25.322
[sighs]

14:25.406 --> 14:26.782
Man, I'm hungry.

14:27.491 --> 14:28.701
Shall we go eat?

14:31.620 --> 14:33.205
Do you wanna talk about work?

14:33.289 --> 14:34.498
[groans]

14:35.082 --> 14:35.958
[sighs]

14:36.041 --> 14:40.170
How about we talk about
that thing you mentioned. A raise, right?

14:41.839 --> 14:44.049
[intrigued music]

14:44.592 --> 14:46.260
What about a raise?

14:47.261 --> 14:49.346
[groans, clears throat]

14:53.225 --> 14:56.520
Anyway, I'll be
watching over you, you two.

14:59.481 --> 15:01.609
- I want 30 percent.
- What?

15:03.444 --> 15:05.154
Okay, 25 percent.

15:05.237 --> 15:07.448
[cheeky music]

15:09.575 --> 15:10.409
20.

15:12.620 --> 15:13.871
[scrapes]

15:23.547 --> 15:24.673
[phone buzzing]

15:30.179 --> 15:31.513
[Ung] Have you eaten?

15:31.597 --> 15:34.558
[Yeon-su] Yes, I have. You should eat too.

15:37.102 --> 15:38.604
UNG

15:38.687 --> 15:40.064
- [Ung] What are you doing?
- [Yeon-su] I'm meeting.

15:40.147 --> 15:41.649
- [Ung] I'm at a restaurant.
- [Yeon-su] Okay.

15:41.732 --> 15:44.443
- [Ung] Did you finish work?
- [Yeon-su] Not yet. I'll be done soon.

15:44.526 --> 15:45.861
YES, OKAY, NOT TODAY

15:46.362 --> 15:48.656
Were my replies too simple?

15:48.739 --> 15:50.908
YOUR NEW SIDE

15:51.492 --> 15:55.204
[Yeon-su] If I want to find a new side,
then I need to learn from new people.

15:55.871 --> 15:58.248
Dating? Well, it's no big deal.

15:58.332 --> 16:00.751
If a man and a woman like each other,
they date,

16:00.834 --> 16:03.253
and the, well, they both kiss,

16:03.337 --> 16:04.505
and then…

16:05.089 --> 16:07.091
[drumming]

16:10.636 --> 16:12.930
And then they say, "I love you."

16:13.013 --> 16:14.056
[sighs]

16:14.139 --> 16:16.225
[Yeon-su] No, that's not a good example.

16:18.852 --> 16:21.105
Did you enjoy your lunch today, Ms. Kook?

16:21.188 --> 16:22.731
Oh, yes.

16:25.609 --> 16:27.653
[bright music]

16:31.657 --> 16:32.908
Hey, Ye-in.

16:32.992 --> 16:33.993
Yes?

16:34.576 --> 16:36.704
- Do you have a boyfriend?
- Me?

16:37.871 --> 16:41.166
I don't, why? Is there someone
you wanna set me up with?

16:41.959 --> 16:44.294
Then did you have any boyfriends before?

16:44.962 --> 16:47.631
Mm. Of course I did.

16:47.715 --> 16:49.675
A had quite a lot back then.

16:50.509 --> 16:51.468
So…

16:52.094 --> 16:56.181
would you…
consider yourself to be good at dating?

16:56.765 --> 16:57.850
[chuckles]

16:58.434 --> 17:01.520
Well, it might seem weird
for me to say this,

17:01.603 --> 17:04.398
but if I were evaluated
for my ability in dating,

17:04.481 --> 17:08.777
I guess I would be the CEO
of this company by now.

17:08.861 --> 17:10.946
- Oh.
- Why do you ask?

17:12.865 --> 17:13.741
Well…

17:16.160 --> 17:20.748
How exactly do you date a person properly?

17:22.666 --> 17:24.835
[upbeat music]

17:24.918 --> 17:27.296
Well, I think you came
to the right place, Ms. Kook.

17:32.509 --> 17:33.427
[groans]

17:37.264 --> 17:38.515
[sighs]

17:40.517 --> 17:41.685
[phone buzzing]

17:45.439 --> 17:48.859
[Yeon-su] I'm getting off of work soon.
Shall we go on a date?

17:49.359 --> 17:51.695
[Ung] Okay. I'll pick you up. Wait there.

17:52.488 --> 17:54.948
[bright music]

17:56.283 --> 17:57.743
[deep sigh]

18:05.959 --> 18:10.297
SUPERB CREATIVE CENTER

18:10.380 --> 18:12.716
[line trilling]

18:14.802 --> 18:17.137
[bright music continues]

18:21.683 --> 18:22.810
[chuckles]

18:24.061 --> 18:24.895
Hi there.

18:28.565 --> 18:29.858
Oh, hi.

18:30.609 --> 18:33.362
Oh, wait.
You're wearing different clothes.

18:33.445 --> 18:37.699
Oh, I accidentally spilled something
so I bought new clothes.

18:37.783 --> 18:39.952
Oh. Did you spill a lot or something?

18:40.828 --> 18:42.287
- Let's go.
- Hmm.

18:53.549 --> 18:57.094
Firstly, visual stimulation
is very important.

18:57.177 --> 19:00.264
You have to show different styles
every now and then so that

19:00.347 --> 19:03.267
you can get a kind of tension
flowing between you two.

19:05.185 --> 19:06.353
[groans]

19:10.065 --> 19:11.275
[both chuckling]

19:11.775 --> 19:12.901
[button clicks]

19:13.861 --> 19:15.988
[engine ignites, revs]

19:17.281 --> 19:18.282
[Ung sighs]

19:18.365 --> 19:20.993
You know what, I still think
it would have been much better

19:21.076 --> 19:22.786
to just hit Eun-ho with a brick.

19:22.870 --> 19:25.455
Ugh, it was hard
having to deal with his sulking.

19:26.123 --> 19:29.084
[Ye-in]  Now this is very, very important.

19:29.168 --> 19:33.505
Reaction. I found out that guys are crazy
for people who give good reactions.

19:33.589 --> 19:36.258
I dated so many guys using my reactions.

19:36.341 --> 19:38.844
React to what he does. And always smile.

19:38.927 --> 19:41.930
Now why in the world would he be so sulky?

19:42.014 --> 19:44.141
I swear, sometimes
he can be so weird, you know.

19:44.224 --> 19:45.976
- [Ung] He must like me so much--
- Oh!

19:46.518 --> 19:49.188
- [Yeon-su] Really?
- Huh? Yeah.

19:49.271 --> 19:51.064
[strange giggle]

19:51.148 --> 19:52.191
That's so funny.

19:52.691 --> 19:53.859
What is?

19:55.485 --> 19:56.612
Huh? What's what?

19:56.695 --> 19:58.238
- What?
- Huh?

19:58.322 --> 20:00.115
[awkward music]

20:00.699 --> 20:02.993
And compliment him
as many times as you can.

20:04.411 --> 20:05.787
Hey, you're such a good driver…

20:07.372 --> 20:08.498
Oh, sorry about that.

20:09.208 --> 20:11.418
- [clears throat]
- What did you say? I didn't catch that.

20:11.501 --> 20:12.753
It's nothing.

20:15.839 --> 20:19.176
[Ye-in] They love receiving compliments,
even for the smallest of things.

20:19.259 --> 20:20.260
[gasps dramatically]

20:20.344 --> 20:22.721
You have really large hands.

20:22.804 --> 20:24.306
What? That was random.

20:24.389 --> 20:26.141
You know, they're so big.

20:26.767 --> 20:28.101
As in, they're huge.

20:28.894 --> 20:29.770
- Oh.
- [gasps]

20:31.688 --> 20:32.856
Right.

20:35.150 --> 20:37.736
- [awkward music]
- [awkward chuckle]

20:45.661 --> 20:47.537
[music fades]

20:49.289 --> 20:50.499
You sure about this?

20:50.582 --> 20:52.876
You usually prefer Korean food.

20:52.960 --> 20:55.921
Well, sometimes I crave
for food like this too.

20:56.004 --> 20:57.297
Ah.

20:57.381 --> 21:00.634
I begged you for a month to go eat pasta
when we were in university.

21:00.717 --> 21:03.387
- But you never said yes.
- Wait, really?

21:04.763 --> 21:06.890
Well, people's tastes do change.
[chuckles]

21:07.808 --> 21:08.642
Hmm.

21:09.768 --> 21:12.562
- I'll cut this for you.
- No, I'll do it. It's closer to me anyway.

21:12.646 --> 21:14.106
- No, let me do it.
- No.

21:17.317 --> 21:18.402
- Oh.
- [gasps]

21:19.278 --> 21:21.363
- [icy music]
- [groans]

21:22.364 --> 21:25.617
And nagging.
Nagging is a big no-no, Ms. Kook!

21:26.201 --> 21:28.954
Men especially despise it
when you nag them.

21:29.830 --> 21:30.914
[chuckles awkwardly]

21:31.748 --> 21:32.916
Oh, I'm sorry.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.502
Waiter, can I get
a wet towel over here, please.

21:35.585 --> 21:38.672
It's fine. I'll wipe it myself.
It's okay, really.

21:38.755 --> 21:43.468
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Uh, are you sure it'll come off?

21:43.552 --> 21:45.345
It's fine. I'll just have it dry cleaned.

21:45.429 --> 21:47.347
[sighs]
Why did it have to fly there?

21:47.431 --> 21:48.849
- [Ung] You should've put…
- You should've just…

21:49.683 --> 21:52.561
I mean, I mean this.
I should have put this here.

21:53.770 --> 21:55.147
It was my bad.

21:55.981 --> 21:58.525
- [awkward chuckle]
- [deep sigh]

22:00.027 --> 22:01.653
- Hey, Ung.
- Huh?

22:01.737 --> 22:04.323
- Eat up, now. Ah.
- Oh.

22:06.116 --> 22:07.909
- Is it good?
- Hmm.

22:08.577 --> 22:09.995
- [chuckles]
- [Yeon-su] Hm.

22:10.078 --> 22:12.164
[bright music]

22:17.419 --> 22:18.754
- [cup thuds]
- [sighs]

22:19.588 --> 22:20.672
[music stops]

22:24.760 --> 22:25.635
[Ung sighs]

22:27.929 --> 22:29.598
What are you thinking about?

22:29.681 --> 22:31.725
It's been a long while
since we walked like this

22:31.808 --> 22:34.227
instead of running after each other.

22:34.311 --> 22:35.145
What?

22:36.146 --> 22:40.275
You used to say that walking
without a purpose was too inefficient,

22:40.358 --> 22:42.527
that's why we always ran around back then.

22:43.528 --> 22:45.739
- Did I really say that?
- Hmm.

22:46.531 --> 22:49.326
I think we were the only ones
who ran around Deoksugung Palace.

22:49.409 --> 22:50.744
[scoffs]

22:50.827 --> 22:53.830
I was really obsessed
with efficiency back then.

22:53.914 --> 22:55.373
It was messy.

22:56.583 --> 22:59.044
That's not true. You were so cool.

23:00.420 --> 23:02.047
[Ye-in] And the last thing you must do…

23:02.130 --> 23:05.217
is to make sure you make
a romantic vibe every chance you get.

23:05.300 --> 23:07.010
Dating is all about

23:07.844 --> 23:09.304
having butterflies.

23:14.643 --> 23:15.602
[Yeon-su clears throat]

23:16.812 --> 23:19.940
By the way,
there's not a lot of people here.

23:21.191 --> 23:23.652
You're right.
It's not even that late yet, though.

23:24.236 --> 23:26.530
How is it that there's nobody around here?

23:28.031 --> 23:30.075
[cheeky music]

23:31.660 --> 23:32.619
Oh…

23:37.707 --> 23:39.751
[cheeky music continues]

23:43.380 --> 23:45.006
Ah. Ow.

23:45.090 --> 23:47.384
What was that for?

23:48.927 --> 23:51.638
- What are you doing, Yeon-su?
- What do you mean?

23:51.721 --> 23:55.058
What's gotten into you today?
What's this character you're playing?

23:56.476 --> 23:58.520
[inhales]
You've been acting so weird all day.

23:59.938 --> 24:01.565
What is it that you're plotting?

24:01.648 --> 24:03.316
I'm not plotting anything.

24:03.400 --> 24:06.027
- I was just making an effort, that's all.
- What effort?

24:06.945 --> 24:09.614
I'm was trying to make
this relationship go well.

24:09.698 --> 24:10.657
Huh?

24:11.241 --> 24:13.410
Can't you see that
I'm trying to change for you

24:13.493 --> 24:15.829
so that we'll stop fighting
like we did before?

24:15.912 --> 24:18.081
Why do you have to do that?

24:18.165 --> 24:19.916
So that we won't ever break up.

24:20.542 --> 24:22.961
[Yeon-su] They say that
couples who fight and break up often

24:23.044 --> 24:24.671
have a higher chance of breaking up again.

24:24.754 --> 24:28.842
And that they know each other so much
that they have no expectations.

24:28.925 --> 24:30.343
Who said that?

24:30.427 --> 24:33.305
Dr. Yoo Yeong, Hankook University's
relationship psychologist.

24:33.805 --> 24:34.890
But that person doesn't know you.

24:36.391 --> 24:37.267
What?

24:37.350 --> 24:40.228
There are so many people like you
who are always different each time.

24:41.813 --> 24:44.399
You always feel new. And different.

24:44.482 --> 24:46.610
You're different
from when I saw you yesterday.

24:48.653 --> 24:49.905
That's not what I mean.

24:49.988 --> 24:51.865
[Ung] See? Another side.

24:51.948 --> 24:54.409
- You're different from three seconds ago.
- Stop.

24:55.368 --> 24:57.537
I never thought
that you were so predictable.

24:57.621 --> 25:00.624
I mean, if that were possible,
I'd be the one with a Ph. D. here.

25:02.292 --> 25:04.044
Okay, but still,

25:04.127 --> 25:07.214
I felt I've always been
such a nag with you

25:07.297 --> 25:10.258
and that I was always the one
starting the fights between us,

25:10.342 --> 25:12.510
so I was trying to stop that.

25:14.095 --> 25:16.640
I like you for who you are.

25:18.225 --> 25:21.102
I like that you always have
new things to nag about.

25:22.437 --> 25:23.647
[chuckles softly]

25:23.730 --> 25:26.608
Even so, I don't want to hear
the same nagging.

25:27.525 --> 25:29.903
You'll have to come up with new things
for the rest of your life.

25:30.820 --> 25:31.905
Do you mean that?

25:33.698 --> 25:35.700
[deep sigh]

25:36.284 --> 25:38.203
I guess this means I ruined our date.

25:38.286 --> 25:39.579
It can start over.

25:40.372 --> 25:42.207
Okay. So why don't we go do
what you want now?

25:43.625 --> 25:45.043
All right. Let's go.

25:45.961 --> 25:48.338
[gentle music]

25:52.884 --> 25:54.594
Guide me to Hwiyeong-dong, please.

25:54.678 --> 25:56.680
GUIDE ME TO HWIYEONG-DONG PLEASE

25:56.763 --> 25:59.933
We're going back home now?
You don't want to do anything else?

26:00.016 --> 26:00.976
There is.

26:03.728 --> 26:06.731
[gentle music continues]

26:12.195 --> 26:13.405
[sighs]

26:15.073 --> 26:18.493
- Is this what you wanted to do?
- Hmm, I love this the most.

26:19.202 --> 26:22.122
Going to the neighborhood pub
in the middle of cold weather

26:22.205 --> 26:25.000
and chatting the night away
over hot fishcake stew.

26:25.083 --> 26:27.252
You're right. I love this the most too.

26:27.335 --> 26:28.753
[both chuckling]

26:30.171 --> 26:31.589
You two are ridiculous.

26:31.673 --> 26:35.593
If you're going to shamelessly
stay here all night over one menu item,

26:35.677 --> 26:37.679
at least give the pub owner a glance.

26:38.513 --> 26:41.182
Sol-i, this is kind of spicy.
Ung can't eat spicy food.

26:41.266 --> 26:42.892
Mm. I'll be fine.

26:42.976 --> 26:44.853
I got used to it
after eating with Yeon-su.

26:44.936 --> 26:47.772
- How about something not spicy?
- Uh, okay…

26:47.856 --> 26:49.316
Order what you wanna eat, Yeon-su.

26:50.150 --> 26:52.527
[all chuckling]

26:52.610 --> 26:55.780
Wow. You're the first customers
that make me wanna puke.

26:55.864 --> 26:56.865
[Sol-i gags]

26:56.948 --> 26:59.117
Good job holding it in, Sol-i.

26:59.200 --> 27:00.201
Hang in there.

27:01.202 --> 27:03.204
[Sol-i] Business isn't easy, you know.

27:03.288 --> 27:04.539
You got this, Sol-i.

27:05.332 --> 27:07.500
[cheerful music]

27:10.962 --> 27:11.880
[sighs]

27:15.675 --> 27:17.177
- [Yeon-su] You want a fish cake?
- Hmm.

27:17.260 --> 27:18.136
Here.

27:20.680 --> 27:22.390
- [Yeon-su] Careful.
- It looks good.

27:22.474 --> 27:24.434
[Ung] All right.

27:25.894 --> 27:27.479
[blows]

27:29.606 --> 27:31.191
- Is it hot?
- [chuckles]

27:31.983 --> 27:33.068
[both chuckling]

27:35.904 --> 27:37.697
[music fades]

27:38.615 --> 27:39.741
[sighs]

27:46.247 --> 27:47.207
[gasps]

27:48.041 --> 27:50.960
You startled me.
What do you want, Grandma?

27:51.044 --> 27:52.879
When did you get home last night?

27:54.047 --> 27:55.423
I don't really know.

27:55.507 --> 27:58.343
You little brat!
[groans]

28:00.470 --> 28:02.722
Were you with Ung
the entire time last night?

28:03.598 --> 28:05.183
Well, I was.

28:05.266 --> 28:08.269
But I didn't arrive home
that late, Grandma. Honest.

28:08.353 --> 28:11.981
Are you really going to go
all the way with him?

28:12.065 --> 28:14.109
What? How can you say that, Grandma?

28:14.192 --> 28:16.945
I'm always going to stay here
by your side.

28:17.028 --> 28:18.780
Stop goofing around, will you?

28:19.364 --> 28:22.283
Listen, if you really want to be together
with Choi Ung that much,

28:22.367 --> 28:24.077
then you just bring him here instead.

28:24.160 --> 28:26.913
Grandma, you'll only
make him uncomfortable, you know.

28:26.996 --> 28:29.332
Last time I brought him here,
you totally bullied him.

28:29.416 --> 28:33.628
Well, that's because I was trying to know
what he thinks about your relationship.

28:33.711 --> 28:35.964
Why are you so old-fashioned, Grandma?

28:36.047 --> 28:38.174
You're getting ahead of yourself. Hm.

28:38.258 --> 28:39.592
I'm taking a shower.

28:40.260 --> 28:44.472
Oh, and don't even think
about going to see Ung. Okay?

28:44.556 --> 28:47.225
'Cause I'll die of embarrassment
if you do that.

28:47.809 --> 28:48.810
What the…

28:49.644 --> 28:52.147
How dare she talk to me like that?

28:52.856 --> 28:54.190
[deep sigh]

28:54.274 --> 28:56.735
Mm-hmm. You should head to work.
You'll be late.

28:56.818 --> 28:58.945
Don't make me drink on a weekday again.

28:59.028 --> 29:02.699
Oh? Hey, you were the one who asked
to drink another bottle at the end.

29:02.782 --> 29:04.826
Stop. Don't ever mention last night.

29:05.493 --> 29:08.788
- I should get going now. See you around.
- Okay.

29:11.374 --> 29:12.417
[groans]

29:14.335 --> 29:15.587
[groans]

29:21.426 --> 29:22.677
[cap rasps]

29:28.933 --> 29:30.018
[sighs]

29:45.492 --> 29:46.701
[sighs]

29:52.373 --> 29:53.875
[phone buzzing]

29:53.958 --> 29:56.669
[groaning]

30:00.924 --> 30:02.008
[sighs]

30:03.384 --> 30:04.594
[groans]

30:13.728 --> 30:15.939
[Ung] I saw the interview you did.

30:16.523 --> 30:18.316
And the article that came out today.

30:18.399 --> 30:22.487
I thought I should at least thank you
for being so considerate and thoughtful.

30:22.570 --> 30:24.697
So, thank you, NJ.

30:24.781 --> 30:27.283
He's drawing a line between us again.

30:30.286 --> 30:31.371
[huffs in annoyance]

30:38.670 --> 30:41.005
[cheeky music]

30:45.260 --> 30:46.678
[groans]

30:51.891 --> 30:53.893
[cheeky music continues]

30:56.187 --> 30:59.941
I finally got one text after so many days,
and you wanna call him right away?

31:00.984 --> 31:02.610
There's no way I'm that cheap.

31:03.319 --> 31:05.572
Let's just ignore that, shall we?

31:09.951 --> 31:11.578
[huffs]

31:19.919 --> 31:22.297
[gasps, groans]

31:22.380 --> 31:23.673
[deep steadying breath]

31:25.133 --> 31:27.302
[cheeky music]

31:29.137 --> 31:30.263
Oh, darn it.

31:30.889 --> 31:32.891
[whining]

31:40.440 --> 31:42.775
[cheeky music]

31:51.659 --> 31:53.745
[cheeky music continues]

31:57.165 --> 32:00.126
Come on, Dad,
why did you order so many cabbages?

32:00.835 --> 32:03.338
Well, why else do you think I did, huh?

32:03.421 --> 32:05.590
It's the season of making kimchi.
Did you forget that?

32:05.673 --> 32:07.467
Oh, that's right. I forgot.

32:07.550 --> 32:10.595
I think I have a fever,
I need to go home and rest.

32:10.678 --> 32:12.180
Oh, okay.

32:12.263 --> 32:13.473
Go on home and rest.

32:13.556 --> 32:15.224
[Ho] But make sure you come back tomorrow.

32:15.308 --> 32:16.893
That's when the cabbages will be here.

32:16.976 --> 32:20.605
Oh, man. Are you making kimchi
for the entire neighborhood?

32:20.688 --> 32:22.857
Hey, Dad. I think you should downsize.

32:22.941 --> 32:24.525
Downsize your restaurants too.

32:24.609 --> 32:27.570
Your business will fail if you keep
trying to many things at once.

32:27.654 --> 32:31.616
What are you going on about?
Business is booming right now, son.

32:31.699 --> 32:33.534
What are you going to do
with all that money?

32:33.618 --> 32:35.036
Are you going to take it with you?

32:35.119 --> 32:36.621
I will do M.A.L.F.Y.

32:37.205 --> 32:39.123
[Ho] Don't you worry about a thing, Ung.

32:39.207 --> 32:42.794
I'll be sure to take
every single cent. You can count on it.

32:44.253 --> 32:45.672
Hey, Mom, do you agree with this?

32:45.755 --> 32:48.132
About this family's legacy?

32:48.216 --> 32:51.928
Well, I'm not sure
about handing it down to you.

32:52.011 --> 32:56.349
Huh? But I'm the only one
who can inherit it. How can you not know?

32:56.432 --> 32:59.727
I think we can trust Yeon-su
to take care of it, am I right?

32:59.811 --> 33:04.065
Yup, that's right. We can trust Yeon-su
to do a much better job than you.

33:04.148 --> 33:05.608
Hmm.

33:05.692 --> 33:06.901
You're so harsh.

33:06.985 --> 33:08.861
Are you saying
you like Yeon-su more than me?

33:08.945 --> 33:09.862
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

33:10.655 --> 33:11.531
That's too bad.

33:12.907 --> 33:14.909
Because she likes me.

33:14.993 --> 33:16.411
[Ung slurps]

33:17.453 --> 33:19.872
I can't believe what I just heard.

33:19.956 --> 33:22.542
I heard it too.
I almost caused an accident.

33:22.625 --> 33:24.544
In fact, I nearly puked on my son's face.

33:25.420 --> 33:26.295
[chuckles]

33:27.964 --> 33:30.967
Tell Yeon-su to come over for dinner
when she gets off work.

33:31.050 --> 33:32.051
No, wait a minute.

33:32.635 --> 33:34.387
She might feel pressured by us.

33:34.971 --> 33:37.473
Right. She'll feel pressured
if we keep asking her over.

33:37.557 --> 33:39.308
Should we pack her some side dishes?

33:39.392 --> 33:41.602
[Yeon-ok] That's way she'll have
something to eat with her grandmother.

33:41.686 --> 33:43.604
No, we'll drop by next time.

33:43.688 --> 33:45.773
Yeon-su said she wanted
to eat your braised fish again.

33:45.857 --> 33:47.483
[gasps]
Really? Woo-hoo!

33:47.567 --> 33:48.860
Then tell me when you'll come.

33:48.943 --> 33:51.112
I'll make sure
it's fresh and delicious, just for her.

33:51.946 --> 33:53.448
Does that mean
I should go to the market tomorrow?

33:54.032 --> 33:54.866
Hold on.

33:54.949 --> 33:58.286
Should I get her some side dishes?

33:58.786 --> 34:00.872
[music fades]

34:04.375 --> 34:05.793
Did she leave the lights on?

34:07.754 --> 34:10.214
LEEZAKAYA

34:14.010 --> 34:14.927
Sol-i?

34:15.928 --> 34:16.929
Sol-i, are you here?

34:17.847 --> 34:19.390
[Sol-i] Who is that? Eun-ho?

34:19.474 --> 34:21.100
Oh, you're still in.

34:21.184 --> 34:22.810
I thought you said you're closed today.

34:22.894 --> 34:26.481
[Sol-i] Yeah. I'm just came in here
to organize some things, that's all.

34:26.564 --> 34:27.690
What are you doing here?

34:27.774 --> 34:31.069
I saw the lights were on from outside,
I thought you forgot to turn them off.

34:31.152 --> 34:33.446
[Sol-i] Hey, don't treat me
like I'm some old lady.

34:33.529 --> 34:35.573
I don't forget things that often.

34:35.656 --> 34:38.159
I turned off the lights for you
five times this month.

34:38.951 --> 34:40.953
I do appreciate that…

34:41.037 --> 34:42.080
[spits violently]

34:42.163 --> 34:44.499
[cheeky music]

34:44.582 --> 34:47.085
Rude. Way too rude.

34:47.168 --> 34:49.253
Spitting out water in front of me?

34:49.337 --> 34:52.924
Oh… Why… why are you dressed like that?

34:53.633 --> 34:55.593
Okay, repeat after me.

34:55.676 --> 34:58.971
"Sol-i, why do you look
prettier than usual?"

35:00.014 --> 35:01.808
[Eun-ho] Where are you going?

35:01.891 --> 35:03.935
What's going on? You're scaring me.

35:04.018 --> 35:07.688
I never thought that
my blind date outfit would ever scare you.

35:07.772 --> 35:09.732
A blind date? You're going on a date?

35:13.236 --> 35:14.362
Who are you going out with?

35:14.445 --> 35:16.864
I don't know yet. My dad's setting me up.

35:17.490 --> 35:19.408
Although I hear he's handsome.

35:20.451 --> 35:21.619
So it's all good.

35:23.287 --> 35:26.457
If your dad's setting you up,
I guess he wants you to marry him.

35:26.999 --> 35:28.543
There's no pressure.

35:31.379 --> 35:34.215
I guess it must feel pretty awkward, huh?

35:34.799 --> 35:37.677
Why awkward? I think it'll be really fun.

35:37.760 --> 35:40.263
How is it fun to eat
with someone you don't know?

35:40.346 --> 35:43.057
Because I love meeting strangers.
It's pretty fun.

35:43.141 --> 35:46.018
Still awkward.
And there's nothing to talk about.

35:46.102 --> 35:49.438
How do I put this? It's my calling.

35:49.522 --> 35:52.233
I have made such good connections
with the people I've just met.

35:52.859 --> 35:54.986
I'd say the flow is incredible.

35:56.028 --> 35:58.698
[cheeky music]

36:01.117 --> 36:02.952
Hey, I see your mouth.

36:03.619 --> 36:06.455
Okay, tell me.
Why are you pouting this time?

36:06.539 --> 36:10.042
If you keep acting like that,
you'll make me misunderstand you.

36:10.126 --> 36:13.546
I used to be a romance screen writer.
So don't mess with me.

36:15.381 --> 36:17.341
What kind of misunderstanding, huh?

36:17.425 --> 36:20.678
Wow, look at you trying to act naive.

36:20.761 --> 36:23.139
I think I already told you about 35 times.

36:24.432 --> 36:26.184
I don't date younger guys.

36:31.606 --> 36:33.649
[charged music]

36:34.525 --> 36:37.904
Yeah, I know that.
This is my 35th rejection.

36:37.987 --> 36:39.155
Hm?

36:43.618 --> 36:46.037
Go ahead.
You go and have fun with your date.

36:47.997 --> 36:49.457
Oh… okay.

36:51.918 --> 36:55.546
Hold on, let me ask. How old is that guy?

36:56.297 --> 37:00.092
- He's much older than me.
- What's so good about an old guy?

37:03.429 --> 37:05.348
- [door closes]
- What a rude brat.

37:09.310 --> 37:10.895
- [knocking]
- Yeah?

37:13.314 --> 37:15.900
I'm taking orders for lunch.
Want anything?

37:15.983 --> 37:17.693
[Ji-ung] I'm fine. You can eat without me.

37:18.486 --> 37:21.155
- But still you…
- I said I'm fine.

37:21.989 --> 37:23.032
All right.

37:23.741 --> 37:25.034
[door closes]

37:31.207 --> 37:32.500
[knocking on door]

37:34.669 --> 37:36.629
Hey, you should at least have dinner.

37:36.712 --> 37:39.507
I don't want to eat.
Thanks for asking, though.

37:40.299 --> 37:41.342
But even so--

37:41.425 --> 37:43.803
Don't worry.
I'll eat something later, I promise.

37:44.804 --> 37:46.931
[soft sigh, smacks lips]

37:51.394 --> 37:52.603
[door closes]

37:58.651 --> 38:00.361
[knocking on door]

38:00.444 --> 38:01.362
[sighs]

38:04.156 --> 38:05.992
[Ji-ung] I said I'm not hungry.

38:06.075 --> 38:08.869
[Yeon-su] Even so,
you should still eat something, Mr. Kim.

38:13.374 --> 38:15.668
[soft gentle music]

38:16.585 --> 38:18.379
I came to see if you were really that busy

38:18.462 --> 38:21.549
or if you were just pretending
so you could get away from me.

38:22.133 --> 38:24.552
I didn't think you would go
as far as skipping meals.

38:25.553 --> 38:28.222
- How'd you get in here?
- I took a taxi, of course.

38:28.306 --> 38:29.765
[sighs]
That's not what I meant--

38:29.849 --> 38:31.684
Well, you should have
answered my messages then.

38:32.810 --> 38:34.603
Are you too busy?
Should I go wait outside?

38:34.687 --> 38:36.439
Oh, no. I'm fine.

38:37.273 --> 38:39.108
All right then. Let's go eat dinner.

38:41.610 --> 38:42.486
Get up now.

38:42.570 --> 38:44.155
[groans]

38:47.033 --> 38:49.452
Can you wait outside for a second?

38:49.535 --> 38:50.494
Okay.

38:51.120 --> 38:53.205
[light emotional music]

38:55.875 --> 38:58.252
[shaky exhale]

39:01.255 --> 39:04.383
[Yeon-su] Wow.
I wish our company had a cafeteria.

39:04.467 --> 39:05.843
You're so lucky.

39:08.512 --> 39:10.014
[indistinct chatter]

39:15.227 --> 39:16.228
[hums in approval]

39:16.312 --> 39:18.189
This is good.

39:18.272 --> 39:21.192
How come you don't eat
all this delicious food? What a waste.

39:21.275 --> 39:24.028
If I worked here,
I'd be eating every single meal here.

39:24.111 --> 39:25.237
[cutlery clicking]

39:29.909 --> 39:32.578
By the way, you look like
you lost some weight.

39:33.120 --> 39:34.663
You really haven't been eating?

39:35.581 --> 39:38.584
Tae-hun told me you've been
living in the editing room lately.

39:39.919 --> 39:41.629
Well, I've been busy these days.

39:42.505 --> 39:45.091
I guess being a producer is really tough.

39:45.174 --> 39:48.219
Still, you should eat properly.
We're not young anymore, after all.

39:48.302 --> 39:49.345
Mm.

39:52.306 --> 39:54.141
So why did you come here?

39:55.351 --> 39:59.313
Oh, well, I wanted to ask
if we could check the footage.

39:59.397 --> 40:02.316
Because the footage that you took
about Soen and our project

40:02.400 --> 40:04.485
should have to be checked
with our client first.

40:07.321 --> 40:10.908
- Okay, I'll send it to you.
- Can't I just see it while I'm still here?

40:11.409 --> 40:12.952
I admit, I'm a bit curious.

40:14.120 --> 40:16.372
Um, I don't have much to show you.

40:16.455 --> 40:18.916
I heard the draft for episode one is out.

40:18.999 --> 40:21.168
I haven't made the revisions yet.
[chuckles awkwardly]

40:26.132 --> 40:28.384
- Hey, Ji-ung.
- Hmm?

40:28.968 --> 40:30.511
Why aren't you looking at me?

40:35.724 --> 40:37.810
[soft vulnerable music]

40:44.483 --> 40:46.152
I look awful right now.

40:46.235 --> 40:47.445
[soft chuckle]

40:47.528 --> 40:50.489
And why would you be worried about that?

40:50.573 --> 40:52.032
Remember your birthday?

40:52.116 --> 40:54.910
I hung out with you
even when my eyes were all swollen.

40:55.744 --> 40:57.288
I hope you didn't forget.

40:57.913 --> 40:58.956
Right.

40:59.039 --> 41:00.082
[soft chuckle]

41:05.296 --> 41:06.714
So, how have you been?

41:08.382 --> 41:11.135
Um. I've been okay.

41:14.305 --> 41:16.891
[chuckles softly]
Same as usual.

41:17.766 --> 41:20.352
And you? Have you been well?

41:20.936 --> 41:23.647
Same as usual for me too.

41:23.731 --> 41:24.732
[soft chuckle]

41:25.983 --> 41:28.194
[soft music continues]

41:33.032 --> 41:34.783
[groans]

41:35.868 --> 41:40.039
If I ignore his messages, I'll just seem
even more pathetic and uncool.

41:40.122 --> 41:42.791
I'll just answer him casually,

41:42.875 --> 41:44.418
make it look like I'm fine.

41:45.544 --> 41:46.378
Oh, no.

41:47.630 --> 41:50.007
How deep did I put that thing? Oh!

41:50.633 --> 41:53.469
I should think before I do anything!

41:54.595 --> 41:56.388
[phone buzzing in pot]

41:56.472 --> 41:57.640
[gasps]

42:01.602 --> 42:02.853
[phone buzzing]

42:03.646 --> 42:06.440
Oh, I give up.

42:07.358 --> 42:09.568
[cheeky music]

42:12.363 --> 42:15.282
- Hey, it seems quite late already.
- Uh.

42:17.952 --> 42:19.995
It's still so early, though.

42:20.079 --> 42:22.289
I guess I had so fun talking to you

42:22.373 --> 42:23.999
that I did not notice the time.

42:25.042 --> 42:26.627
I never expected

42:26.710 --> 42:29.838
that I'd have so much fun
going out on a blind date with someone.

42:29.922 --> 42:31.715
[chuckles]
Right?

42:32.466 --> 42:36.303
If it's okay, I would like
to talk with you a little more.

42:37.096 --> 42:38.347
[chuckles softly]

42:39.056 --> 42:40.516
I would love that.

42:41.600 --> 42:42.851
Where do you wanna go?

42:43.978 --> 42:46.605
- There's a place with clam stew--
- How about a cafe?

42:46.689 --> 42:49.066
A cafe sounds nice. Sure, let's go.

42:50.067 --> 42:50.901
Oh, wait.

42:50.985 --> 42:52.903
- Were you saying something earlier?
- No.

42:52.987 --> 42:53.862
[awkward chuckle]

42:53.946 --> 42:55.614
The clam stew…

42:56.407 --> 42:58.158
[dawning music]

42:58.242 --> 43:00.703
[gasps]
The clams!

43:05.499 --> 43:08.669
Oh, man. Did I forget to lock up again?

43:09.253 --> 43:11.130
[groans]
What is wrong with me?

43:12.047 --> 43:13.632
Now where are those clams?

43:14.383 --> 43:15.843
- [screams]
- [Eun-ho] Oh, my goodness!

43:15.926 --> 43:18.304
You startled me, Sol-i. Why did you shout?

43:18.387 --> 43:20.264
What the heck was that, huh?

43:20.347 --> 43:23.309
What do you mean? What are you doing here?

43:23.392 --> 43:26.270
You see what I mean?
You forgot about all these clams.

43:26.812 --> 43:28.063
Did you bring these inside?

43:28.147 --> 43:29.607
They were just sitting there outside.

43:29.690 --> 43:31.984
I could have ignored them,
but I decided to be nice.

43:32.067 --> 43:33.819
These clams would've died out there

43:33.902 --> 43:36.280
because you were preoccupied
with your date.

43:39.241 --> 43:40.909
[chuckles]

43:44.246 --> 43:45.956
So why are you back early?

43:46.040 --> 43:48.250
You acted like
you were going to have a blast.

43:48.334 --> 43:50.169
[Eun-ho] It wasn't that fun, wasn't it?

43:50.794 --> 43:53.213
Wasn't it awkward
to talk with a guy you just met?

43:57.635 --> 43:59.345
You were right. It was boring.

43:59.428 --> 44:01.555
- [cheeky music]
- [scoffs]

44:01.639 --> 44:04.850
You see what I mean?
There was no way it would be any fun.

44:04.933 --> 44:05.976
[Eun-ho] It was so obvious.

44:06.060 --> 44:09.021
All of your conversations
will just end in silence.

44:09.104 --> 44:10.356
Yeah, you're right.

44:10.439 --> 44:13.567
You know what? You should use that time
to get more customers for this place.

44:13.651 --> 44:15.861
You need to pay back your loan
before you die.

44:16.612 --> 44:17.446
[phone buzzing]

44:18.238 --> 44:20.199
- Told you it'd be boring.
- [clatters]

44:22.493 --> 44:25.120
[date] I had so much fun today.
Can I see you again next time?

44:26.705 --> 44:28.248
- What's that?
- Oh.

44:29.416 --> 44:30.542
An ad for a loan.

44:30.626 --> 44:34.254
I guess they can really smell people
who are desperate for money.

44:34.338 --> 44:36.965
But do they really send ads at this hour?

44:37.049 --> 44:38.592
They sure work hard.

44:38.676 --> 44:40.803
[cheerful music]

44:43.639 --> 44:44.890
Do you want clam stew?

44:47.726 --> 44:49.019
Sol-i!

44:49.103 --> 44:51.647
What is it? Why are you yelling?

44:51.730 --> 44:54.400
Do you think you were going to use
my labor for free?

44:55.067 --> 44:56.276
Outrageous.

44:57.069 --> 45:00.364
Anyway, go to the fridge,
I put some of the clams inside.

45:01.824 --> 45:05.119
All right. I'll make you
an amazing clam stew.

45:07.663 --> 45:10.124
And we'll also empty out
my stock of alcohol.

45:10.207 --> 45:12.960
Oh, what? That sounds a bit scary.

45:13.919 --> 45:15.379
[Eun-ho] Why would we do that?

45:16.672 --> 45:18.549
Hey? Sol-i?

45:19.216 --> 45:20.300
[music stops]

45:24.054 --> 45:24.972
Oh!

45:26.390 --> 45:28.142
I was just about to ring the doorbell.

45:28.225 --> 45:30.936
And I wasn't standing here all night,
so don't get the wrong idea.

45:31.019 --> 45:33.105
Oh, what are you doing here?

45:33.981 --> 45:36.692
I didn't choose to talk
at the interview just for you.

45:36.775 --> 45:38.944
And there was no special meaning to it.

45:39.027 --> 45:42.322
I'm not the kind of person
who'd be so considerate of others.

45:42.406 --> 45:44.616
Oh. Did you come here just to say that?

45:44.700 --> 45:46.118
You could have just
texted me that, you know?

45:46.201 --> 45:47.661
My phone is…

45:48.495 --> 45:51.081
Anyway, it's not what you think.
Do you understand?

45:51.832 --> 45:53.292
You can go inside now.

45:53.375 --> 45:54.793
[groans]
I was on my way out.

45:54.877 --> 45:56.086
Oh, okay.

45:56.170 --> 45:57.463
Yeah.

45:57.546 --> 45:59.631
[awkward music]

46:00.757 --> 46:02.968
Oh, I'm the one who should leave, right?

46:03.719 --> 46:06.638
Wait, since you came all the way here.
Let me make you tea.

46:08.682 --> 46:09.892
Wait.

46:10.642 --> 46:11.518
Well…

46:13.270 --> 46:14.897
Why don't I give you a ride…

46:15.481 --> 46:16.899
No, that'd be strange too.

46:19.776 --> 46:21.278
I guess that means…

46:22.029 --> 46:23.739
we have an awkward relationship.

46:27.075 --> 46:29.661
I promise I won't visit you randomly
like this anymore.

46:30.245 --> 46:31.538
Nor will I text and call you.

46:31.622 --> 46:33.832
Because if you ask me,
I wouldn't want to see another girl

46:33.916 --> 46:37.419
hovering around my man either.
Especially if it's someone like me,

46:37.503 --> 46:39.379
it'd be quite stressful for her,
don't you think?

46:39.463 --> 46:40.797
[both chuckle]

46:41.715 --> 46:43.217
We can be…

46:43.717 --> 46:45.886
Never mind.
We are not going to be friends.

46:45.969 --> 46:48.305
'Cause I actually
don't make friends with guys.

46:48.388 --> 46:50.098
So I'm the one who turned you down.

46:50.682 --> 46:53.143
I'll get going, then.
There's no need for you to see me off.

46:58.565 --> 47:00.901
Also, I didn't really like you
that much anyway.

47:00.984 --> 47:02.027
I only liked you a little.

47:02.110 --> 47:05.072
No, in fact, I don't even have
any feelings for you left at all.

47:07.115 --> 47:10.410
But at least let me tell you this,
just in case.

47:11.119 --> 47:12.788
If you break up again, call me.

47:15.123 --> 47:17.584
[soft vulnerable music]

47:22.339 --> 47:24.049
[footsteps receding]

47:29.680 --> 47:31.431
[Yeon-su] This is so cool.

47:32.099 --> 47:33.934
I've never seen these.

47:36.228 --> 47:39.189
There's really not much to see.
I still have a lot to work on.

47:39.273 --> 47:40.774
No, it's fine, I understand.

47:40.857 --> 47:42.526
So, what do I press?

47:47.489 --> 47:48.824
[Yeon-su groans]

47:48.907 --> 47:50.158
[deep sigh]

47:57.332 --> 47:59.459
[chuckles softly]

48:00.586 --> 48:02.588
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

48:07.551 --> 48:09.011
[soft chuckle]

48:15.392 --> 48:17.060
PACKED MEALS

48:25.444 --> 48:27.946
Hello. Good day, my name is Choi Ung.

48:30.657 --> 48:31.783
And I am…

48:32.534 --> 48:35.120
[Yeon-su groaning]
Do I really have to do this?

48:35.621 --> 48:38.332
So Ung was actually smirking back then.

48:38.415 --> 48:40.500
Gosh, he's so sly.

48:42.586 --> 48:43.795
[Yeon-su] Honestly, though,

48:44.546 --> 48:46.840
- I was a bit worried.
- By the way, I don't know

48:46.923 --> 48:50.844
if it's because of
your filming skills or something else,

48:50.927 --> 48:53.430
- but I look kind of good.
- [both chuckle]

48:55.932 --> 48:57.184
Huh?

48:57.976 --> 48:59.227
When did you take this?

48:59.311 --> 49:01.021
I didn't know you were still filming.

49:03.023 --> 49:05.233
Wow. I admit,

49:06.068 --> 49:07.903
you're pretty good at your job, huh?

49:07.986 --> 49:10.697
You didn't miss a single moment.
[chuckles softly]

49:15.327 --> 49:19.581
Was I really
looking at Ung with that expression?

49:21.208 --> 49:23.752
["Drawer" continuing]

49:26.713 --> 49:28.590
[chuckles]

49:36.640 --> 49:38.934
- Sorry, Yeon-su, but…
- Huh?

49:39.017 --> 49:42.354
- I have to…
- Oh, right. You're busy.

49:42.979 --> 49:46.525
[Yeon-su] Sorry.
I took up too much of your time.

49:48.694 --> 49:50.570
Thanks. I enjoyed the video.

49:50.654 --> 49:54.616
I'll send you the file
to your email later.

49:54.700 --> 49:57.703
Okay. Sure. Take good care of your health.

49:59.413 --> 50:01.915
Let's have a good meal with Ung next time.

50:03.417 --> 50:05.252
I don't think I'll be able to
anytime soon.

50:05.335 --> 50:07.003
Do you want to meet near your home?

50:07.087 --> 50:08.964
- Or at Ung's place, or--
- I need some…

50:11.425 --> 50:12.843
I just need some time.

50:13.593 --> 50:14.428
Huh?

50:16.304 --> 50:18.390
I just need some time, that's all.

50:19.433 --> 50:20.684
Oh.
[chuckles]

50:21.351 --> 50:23.812
All right. We can meet when you're free.

50:24.479 --> 50:25.939
I'll get going now. Bye.

50:30.444 --> 50:31.987
- [deep exhale]
- [door closes]

50:34.239 --> 50:36.199
["Drawer" continuing]

50:49.296 --> 50:50.213
[sighs]

50:57.095 --> 50:58.513
[music stops]

50:58.597 --> 51:01.266
- [distant dog barking]
- [mumbles]

51:04.102 --> 51:05.353
[steadying breath]

51:09.274 --> 51:10.150
[sighs]

51:11.777 --> 51:13.320
[doorbell chiming]

51:18.825 --> 51:22.162
Yeon-su told me that
she'll be coming home late today.

51:23.163 --> 51:25.248
Oh, I'm aware of that.

51:26.666 --> 51:27.834
So…

51:28.543 --> 51:31.546
you came when you knew
that only I'd be here?

51:31.630 --> 51:33.632
- Yes.
- Well.

51:35.050 --> 51:38.303
You always looked like
a scared little puppy whenever you'd come.

51:38.386 --> 51:39.721
What's the occasion now?

51:42.015 --> 51:44.893
Oh. Well, have you had dinner yet?

51:46.228 --> 51:48.730
- I brought some side dishes.
- I just ate.

51:49.523 --> 51:51.024
I see.

51:53.777 --> 51:54.986
Uh…

51:55.987 --> 51:57.697
[sighs]

52:01.159 --> 52:03.161
- No, stay there.
- Oh.

52:03.245 --> 52:04.788
Let me get you some tea.

52:06.748 --> 52:08.166
[deep sigh]

52:11.336 --> 52:12.629
Do you like jujube tea?

52:13.839 --> 52:15.423
I love it very much.

52:15.507 --> 52:17.759
I hate it because it smellsso rotten.

52:18.385 --> 52:21.054
Well, good for you.
You can drink everything then.

52:23.056 --> 52:25.350
- [Ho] Come on. Let's go…
- [Yeon-ok] Right, right.

52:25.433 --> 52:28.019
[Ho] Come on. Let's go.

52:28.103 --> 52:29.187
Oh, Yeon-su!

52:29.771 --> 52:31.273
Oh, my, did you just get off work?

52:31.356 --> 52:34.401
Yes, I'm on my way home now.
Did you just close up?

52:34.484 --> 52:36.903
Yes, we're about to head
back home ourselves.

52:37.487 --> 52:39.865
- [Yeon-ok] Have you eaten?
- Oh, I just ate with Ji-ung earlier.

52:39.948 --> 52:42.659
- Oh, really?
- So how is Ji-ung doing these days?

52:42.742 --> 52:44.244
We haven't seen him in a long time.

52:44.327 --> 52:47.330
He's been pretty busy.
He hasn't left his office.

52:48.039 --> 52:50.375
We should make some side dishes
for Ji-ung too.

52:50.458 --> 52:51.334
Mm-hmm.

52:51.418 --> 52:55.338
Oh, that's right.
Ung brought some side dishes for you.

52:55.422 --> 52:57.716
- Where did he go?
- To your house, silly.

52:57.799 --> 52:59.217
Didn't he tell you about it?

53:00.176 --> 53:02.470
But, only my grandma is home right now…

53:02.554 --> 53:05.390
You should bring your grandmother along
for a meal next time.

53:05.473 --> 53:08.476
- I heard you wanted some braised fish.
- [both laugh]

53:08.560 --> 53:10.729
I do. Yes. I will.

53:10.812 --> 53:12.230
You must be tired.

53:16.484 --> 53:19.029
Hurry on home. Go get some rest.

53:19.821 --> 53:21.823
Okay. Good night, then.

53:21.907 --> 53:25.577
WITH UNG

53:27.746 --> 53:30.040
- Go on. Hurry home.
- [chuckles]

53:32.792 --> 53:34.794
[soft gentle music]

53:43.428 --> 53:44.471
Where are you?

53:45.096 --> 53:46.306
I heard you went to my house.

53:46.389 --> 53:49.142
[Ung] Hmm. I was there. I'm back home now.

53:49.225 --> 53:51.645
Uh. Did you meet with my grandmother?

53:51.728 --> 53:54.064
Did she say anything to you? Or scold you?

53:54.147 --> 53:56.858
Actually, wait. I'll go
to your house right now. Wait right there.

53:58.944 --> 54:00.445
I'll make some tea for you.

54:02.072 --> 54:04.824
So then why did you go to my house
while I wasn't there?

54:04.908 --> 54:06.993
You must have been bullied
by my grandma again.

54:07.077 --> 54:08.036
[Ung] I wasn't.

54:12.832 --> 54:14.960
[Yeon-su] Do you read books
like this lately?

54:16.753 --> 54:19.714
I haven't been reading much lately. Hm.

54:19.798 --> 54:21.174
I should read more too.

54:29.391 --> 54:31.059
ENSA ENROLLMENT FORM

54:31.142 --> 54:32.978
ARTIST GO-OH
MUSEUM OF AVANT-GARDE, PARIS, FRANCE

54:33.061 --> 54:35.230
CONCERNING VARIABILITY
AND INVARIABILITY›

54:35.313 --> 54:36.356
PROGRAMS, ALUMNI, ENROLLMENT

54:36.439 --> 54:37.899
What's this now?

54:37.983 --> 54:39.693
[sighs]
It's nothing.

54:39.776 --> 54:43.321
This kind of looks like a brochure
for an architecture school.

54:43.405 --> 54:45.448
Were you once interested in architecture?

54:45.532 --> 54:48.618
Well, do you remember the architect
I told you I liked?

54:49.369 --> 54:51.871
He's a professor there,
so I was looking at it.

54:51.955 --> 54:54.165
Oh. Oh, well.

54:54.249 --> 54:57.836
You're always drawing buildings, so
of course you would be interested in it.

54:58.336 --> 55:00.463
- I'm really not.
- Why?

55:00.547 --> 55:02.590
I think it would be nice
for you to learn more.

55:02.674 --> 55:04.551
Why would I do that?
[inhales]

55:04.634 --> 55:06.720
It would be such a bother.

55:06.803 --> 55:09.431
Drawing is exhausting enough as it is.

55:10.015 --> 55:10.932
You're right.

55:11.016 --> 55:13.893
Having a university diploma
is already enough.

55:15.895 --> 55:18.023
- What?
- I didn't graduate.

55:19.441 --> 55:20.358
What?

55:21.401 --> 55:22.318
Why?

55:23.361 --> 55:25.363
I thought I didn't really need to.

55:25.447 --> 55:28.199
Wait, Ung, have you lost your mind?

55:28.283 --> 55:31.161
You attended school
and paid for that tuition.

55:31.244 --> 55:33.121
Are you saying that all went to waste?

55:33.788 --> 55:37.584
Well, you know what?
I never wanted to go to university anyway.

55:37.667 --> 55:39.085
I only went because of you.

55:41.838 --> 55:42.964
[chuckles softly]

55:43.048 --> 55:44.841
Hey, why are you so shocked?

55:44.924 --> 55:47.343
You know very well that
I don't like going to school.

55:49.554 --> 55:53.808
Yeah, but still, how could you
just quit so easily like that?

55:54.893 --> 55:57.937
There are people
who don't really need a diploma.

55:59.397 --> 56:01.107
[professor] Is that your reason?

56:01.191 --> 56:03.735
You'll be able to draw
all the buildings you love

56:03.818 --> 56:05.987
and learn much more if you go there.

56:06.071 --> 56:08.448
Give this chance to someone
who needs it more than I do.

56:09.324 --> 56:11.576
[gentle music]

56:14.454 --> 56:17.373
Oh, that's right.
Eun-ho bought some cookies. Hang on.

56:21.127 --> 56:24.881
By the way, I want to know
if Grandma said anything to you?

56:24.964 --> 56:28.093
If she said anything harsh to you,
don't take it personally.

56:28.176 --> 56:29.761
[Yeon-su] It's just her way of talking.

56:36.768 --> 56:37.852
[sighs]

56:38.686 --> 56:41.648
Yeon-su. Can I ask you a question?

56:42.941 --> 56:44.734
Hmm. What is it?

56:47.153 --> 56:47.987
So why…

56:53.993 --> 56:56.246
why did we break up back then?

56:58.373 --> 57:00.542
["Maybe If" by BIBI playing]

57:00.625 --> 57:04.504
♪ The distance between you and me ♪

57:04.587 --> 57:08.591
♪ It never seems to disappear ♪

57:08.675 --> 57:10.802
[singing in Korean]

57:14.139 --> 57:18.935
EPILOGUE

57:23.064 --> 57:26.568
[sighs]
I am so completely messed up.

57:30.238 --> 57:31.614
[Chae-ran] Here, drink this.

57:32.574 --> 57:33.408
Thanks.

57:35.869 --> 57:39.747
[Chae-ran] I saw you two
in the editing room a while ago.

57:39.831 --> 57:41.708
It reminded me of a movie.

57:41.791 --> 57:42.959
A movie?

57:43.042 --> 57:44.544
Love Actually.

57:45.128 --> 57:47.672
The story where the guy likes
his best friend's wife.

57:49.299 --> 57:50.633
You sure that's not Love and War?

57:52.135 --> 57:56.222
In the movie's ending, the guy ends up
confessing his feelings in a sketchbook.

57:57.265 --> 57:59.392
That became it's most famous scene.

58:02.312 --> 58:04.397
What's your ending going to be?

58:06.065 --> 58:07.525
Don't know.

58:07.609 --> 58:09.319
Because mine's not a movie.

58:11.863 --> 58:13.364
It's a documentary.

58:17.577 --> 58:19.787
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

58:23.291 --> 58:26.794
♪ In this moment ♪

58:26.878 --> 58:29.797
♪ I see you ♪

58:30.298 --> 58:35.303
♪ It always comes around as I believed ♪

58:37.096 --> 58:40.391
♪ When the rain stops ♪

58:40.475 --> 58:43.811
♪ You shine on me ♪

58:43.895 --> 58:48.900
♪ Your light's the only thing
That keeps the cold out ♪

58:50.944 --> 58:52.403
[Ho] See, that's what the media does.

58:52.487 --> 58:55.448
It attracts unnecessary attention
as a consequence.

58:55.532 --> 58:56.533
[man] How have you been?

58:56.616 --> 58:58.952
[Ji-ung] By the way,
why don't you have any friends?

58:59.035 --> 59:01.913
Do you actually think
we're in the same situation?

59:02.497 --> 59:04.874
Just so you know,
Sol-i's not yours anymore.

59:04.958 --> 59:07.126
[Ung] What kind of person
do I come off as?

59:07.710 --> 59:10.088
Do I look lost and aimless?

59:10.922 --> 59:12.590
[Yeon-su] That's what
the past does to you.

59:14.092 --> 59:16.344
It causes you to make the same mistakes.

59:16.427 --> 59:20.139
[Ung] You seemed
so desperate to break up with me.
